## Context

During the raid that added `erg log`, `erg new`, and `erg archive`, the
`test_new.sh` file was delivered without wiring `new` into `TEST_SUITES` in
the Makefile. `make test` passed (the suite was silently skipped) but 16 tests
were never exercised. Caught at verify-gate; fixed in the reroll commit.

The anti-pattern: add `tests/test_foo.sh` → forget to add `foo` to
`TEST_SUITES` → CI passes with zero coverage of the new suite.

## Actions

Add a check to `_test-lint` that cross-references `tests/test_*.sh` against
`TEST_SUITES` and exits non-zero if any test file has no matching suite entry.

Something like:
```make
@for f in tests/test_*.sh; do \
    suite=$$(basename $$f .sh | sed 's/^test_//'); \
    echo " $(TEST_SUITES) " | grep -q " $$suite " || \
        { echo "ERROR: $$f not in TEST_SUITES" >&2; exit 1; }; \
done
```

## Exit criteria

- `_test-lint` fails if any `tests/test_X.sh` file lacks a matching `X` in
  `TEST_SUITES`
- `make test` still passes on main
- Adding a new `tests/test_foo.sh` without updating `TEST_SUITES` causes
  `make test` to fail visibly
